{
  "feature": "Locked (never cut), sub-project 5.1",
  "note": "Every surface the lock draws on or changes: the decklist's list view and its Lock cards mode, the card view's tiles, the Shopping list and the card modal's stand-ins door, the review screen's Put back, and the climb's What would have to go sheet.\n\nThe fixture is BUILT, because no account on local-dev holds a lock: `LOCKED_DECK` is a committed copy of a whole template deck carrying three plain locks (one on an auto card, so Clear all auto reports it), a locked Game Changer asked for twice so it lands on the Shopping list (`LOCKED_SHOP_NAME`), and one DORMANT lock on a card cut from the draft, which is what puts a locked row in the review screen's Out column. `LOCKED_CLIMB_DECK` is a copy of the upgrade-path fixture with two of its five Game Changers locked, so the lower rung's sheet draws both the locked candidates and the out-of-reach note.\n\nThe Pull it guard is not photographed here: it needs a SECOND deck holding the card locked, and `probe:review-locks` builds and asserts exactly that. A sheet cell of a row with no Pull it would read as coverage while proving nothing.",
  "rows": [
    {
      "id": "deck-list",
      "label": "/decks/[id] list view: the lock mark after a locked row's name",
      "view": "src/components/decks/decklist-row.tsx",
      "steps": [
        {
          "goto": "/decks/${LOCKED_DECK}",
          "wait": "h1",
          "settle": 3500
        },
        {
          "scrollTo": "[data-testid$=lock-mark]:visible",
          "settle": 500
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lock-mode",
